# Design Tokens

## Color Palette
Never hardcode hex values. Use Tailwind token classes or CSS variables:

| Token | Value | Tailwind Class |
|---|---|---|
| Primary Gold | `#e5a93c` | `text-gold`, `bg-gold`, `border-gold` |
| Primary Dark | `#16130f` | `text-dark`, `bg-dark` |
| Secondary Dark | `#2e271f` | `text-secondary-dark`, `bg-secondary-dark` |

CSS variables available globally:
```css
var(--color-gold)           /* #e5a93c */
var(--color-dark)           /* #16130f */
var(--color-secondary-dark) /* #2e271f */
```

## Typography
Use Tailwind typography classes only — never hardcode `font-family`, `font-size`, or `font-weight`:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<h1 style={{ fontSize: '48px', fontWeight: 700, fontFamily: 'Playfair Display' }}>

// ✅ GOOD
<h1 className="font-display text-4xl font-bold text-dark">
```

## Spacing & Shadows
Use the extended Tailwind scale defined in `tailwind.config.ts` — never raw px/rem values in className strings.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — hardcoded color
<button className="bg-[#e5a93c] text-[#16130f]">

// ✅ GOOD — design token
<button className="bg-gold text-dark">

// ❌ BAD — inline style
<div style={{ color: '#e5a93c' }}>

// ✅ GOOD — CSS variable or token class
<div className="text-gold">
```
